# Research Report: Class Format / Product / Package / Attendance Domain Model

All paths below are on the remote host at `/opt/soulpilates` (there are also `backup-2026-06-30-*` and `backups/patch-*` directories with older copies — I read only the live, non-backup tree unless noted).

---

## 1. `ClassBlueprint.Format`

**File:** `/opt/soulpilates/SoulPilates.Core/Entities/ClassBlueprint.cs:13`

```csharp
public string Format { get; set; } = "GROUP"; // "GROUP", "PRIVATE"
```

- **Not a C# enum** — a plain `string` with a magic-string comment. I confirmed there is no `enum` type anywhere in `SoulPilates.Core/Entities/*.cs` for any Format/Type/Status field (`grep -rn 'enum '` only turns up `ReviewApprovalStatus` in `ReviewUpload.cs:10` and `BookingFunnelStep` in `VisitorEvent.cs:73`, both unrelated). This is consistent with the rest of the schemaless-Mongo codebase — `Status`, `Type`, `FormatRestriction`, etc. are all bare strings.
- **The entity's own comment is stale/incomplete.** It lists only `"GROUP", "PRIVATE"`, but the rest of the codebase (materialiser, admin UI, analytics) treats `ClassBlueprint.Format`/`CalendarSession.Format` as a 3–4 value domain: `GROUP`, `MAT`, `PRIVATE`, and (inconsistently) `DUO`.
- The blueprint editor UI (`/opt/soulpilates/SoulPilates.Astro/src/pages/admin/class-blueprint-form.astro:126-130`) only offers:
  ```html
  <option value="GROUP">Group</option>
  <option value="MAT">Mat Group Classes</option>
  <option value="PRIVATE">Private</option>
  ```
  **No `DUO` option** for blueprints. `SoulPilates.API/Controllers/ClassBlueprintController.cs` (`Create`/`Update` handlers, lines 51-96) does **no server-side allow-list validation** of `Format` — it just persists whatever string is posted — so nothing in the API stops a raw API call from setting `Format="DUO"` on a blueprint, but the UI never does so.
- `DefaultCapacity` (line 17, default `10`) is a single int with **no format-conditional default** in the entity or in the materialiser (`SchedulingService.cs:3641,3815,3887` all just copy `blueprint.DefaultCapacity` straight onto the session; there is no "if PRIVATE then force 1" logic in the blueprint/materialiser layer itself — that clamp happens later, at booking time, on `CalendarSession`, see §2).

### "Duo" search on ClassBlueprint / nearby code
`ClassBlueprint.cs` itself contains **no** mention of Duo. But a broader `grep -rni duo` across the whole repo (excluding backups) returned **28 files** with hits — this is NOT an empty search. See §6 for the full breakdown; the short version is: there is an extensive, already-shipped "Duo Private" feature (ticket **SPM-98**), but it is **not** implemented as a `ClassBlueprint.Format` value — it's a runtime seat-bump on `PRIVATE`-format sessions (§2/§5).

